{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/996184-are-hermetic-acolytes-considered-members-of-the-order-of-hermes","id":996184,"title":"are hermetic acolytes considered members of the order of hermes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T11:55:37-07:00","id":996184,"title":"are hermetic acolytes considered members of the order of hermes?","content":"we know that sorcers(meaning those who have achieved the third degree) are.<br /> <br /> but what about those whose knowledge is only theoretical? meaning no path dots at all.(1st and second degree)&gt;\\?<br /> <br /> yet they have sworn the oath","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:02:19-07:00","id":996189,"title":"","content":"The Oath marks the Initiation into the Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:43:08-07:00","id":996386,"title":"","content":"As much as Sorcerers, every Tradition or Convention have members who lack any special power or talent at all, only partaking from Paradigm. The thing is, on an in-setting perspective, what you need to be of a given group is just Paradigm. Mages are human beings, and any human being can join a cabal or conspiracy and share ideas, knowledge and beliefs. To have actual powers isn't a priority or requisite, though it does indicate accomplishment once in the fold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:44:15-07:00","id":996387,"title":"","content":"To make it clear: as everything else common to the Traditions, the Order of Hermes not only share this take. They <u><i>invented</i></u> it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T19:37:20-07:00","id":996402,"title":"","content":"There is no doubt a huge glass-ceiling for advancement of non-mages, but there are likely plenty of non-mages within the organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T05:03:10-07:00","id":996533,"title":"","content":"Acolytes would likely be stuck at the first degree, and it's not until you finish the apprenticeship and achieve the fourth degree that you are considered a &quot;true&quot; inducted mber of the Order.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Order does prefer their apprentices to start unawakened. Makes them easier to teach if they start from scratch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:34:26-07:00","id":997107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/996184-are-hermetic-acolytes-considered-members-of-the-order-of-hermes?p=996533#post996533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acolytes would likely be stuck at the first degree, and it's not until you finish the apprenticeship and achieve the fourth degree that you are considered a &quot;true&quot; inducted mber of the Order.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Order does prefer their apprentices to start unawakened. Makes them easier to teach if they start from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> technically speaking they can reach the second degree.<br /> <br /> the first degree ends after you have mastered basic hermetic theories. including things that verge on real life sciences. so unless one is a complete idiot(and who nominated him for the order<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />?_<br /> everyone should pass it. eventually<br /> <br /> the second degree starts by studying sorcery but doesn't<b> end</b> until one hs actually achieved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:32:08-07:00","id":997199,"title":"","content":"Well noted, so yes, a pretty common human being can, still, achieve the second degree sooner or later.<br /> <br /> It even means that an actual Mage in the beginning of her learning at the Order can have as teacher a common human that has mastered the theory. The student have the capacity and already enough talent to make the breakthrough the master wasn't able to, but still lack knowledge to evolve properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}